    {
      "id": "375be43e-b9ce-4ed9-9725-0485e43c79f2",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -80,
        -1040
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1160,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "# Session Check-In Kiosk with Attendance Eligibility Alerts\n\nA QR-powered attendance kiosk for cohort programs with a certification attendance requirement. Participants scan a session QR code that opens this form with the session code prefilled, type only their email, and get an instant confirmation screen. Behind the scenes the workflow dedupes double scans, tags walk-ins, timestamps every check-in to Google Sheets, recomputes the cumulative attendance fraction against the required sessions that remain, and alerts Slack the moment the certification threshold becomes mathematically unreachable.\n\n## How it works\n1. A participant scans the session QR code, which opens the production form URL with session_code prefilled as a query parameter. They type only their email.\n2. Workflow Configuration centralizes the Sheet ID, tab names, Slack channel and certification threshold, and builds the email plus session composite key.\n3. The Data Table rowNotExists check screens out double scans. Duplicates route straight to an Already Checked In screen.\n4. First scans are validated against the cohort roster tab. Unregistered walk-ins are tagged WALK_IN and still logged, never rejected.\n5. The check-in row is timestamped to the Check-Ins tab, then the composite key is recorded in the dedupe Data Table.\n6. The cohort schedule tab is read to derive required sessions, and required sessions still ahead are counted from schedule dates later than today.\n7. A Code node recomputes the cumulative attendance fraction and the best case fraction with perfect attendance from here.\n8. If the threshold is mathematically unreachable, a Slack alert names the person and the shortfall. Every branch ends on a form completion screen.\n\n## Setup\n- Replace <__PLACEHOLDER_VALUE__REGISTRATION_SHEET_ID__> in Workflow Configuration with your registration spreadsheet ID.\n- Keep tab names in sync: Cohort Roster (email, name, cohort), Cohort Schedule (cohort, session_code, session_date, required), Check-Ins (checked_in_at, email, name, cohort, session_code, status).\n- Replace <__PLACEHOLDER_VALUE__SLACK_CHANNEL_ID__> with the coordinator channel ID and invite the bot to that channel.\n- Adjust certification_threshold (default 0.8) if your program uses a different bar.\n- The Data Table session_checkin_dedupe is already created and wired by ID. Keep its columns checkin_key, email, session_code, checked_in_at.\n- Publish the workflow, then build QR codes on the PRODUCTION form URL with ?session_code=YOUR_CODE appended."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e49c0e2d-f4ee-4996-816c-4b203e51f680",
      "name": "Production URL warning",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
