    {
      "id": "8b4c6460-a5a6-4d88-becc-7dfdb9c1d452",
      "name": "Section validate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -176,
        304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 816,
        "height": 404,
        "content": "## Validate, tag and log\n\nThe roster tab decides REGISTERED or WALK_IN. Walk-ins are tagged and logged, never rejected. The check-in row is timestamped to the Sheet, then the composite key lands in the dedupe Data Table."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a065b51a-6c7f-40e6-99cc-c5f7932a907f",
      "name": "Section eligibility",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        704,
        304
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1504,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "## Eligibility math and alert\n\nRequired sessions still ahead are derived from schedule dates later than today, not a static count, so the reachability math stays honest mid-program. When even perfect attendance from here cannot reach the threshold, Slack gets an alert naming the person and the shortfall."
